# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is stored LF in the repository and checked out LF on
# every platform. Git still detects binary content for itself and
# leaves it alone, so this stays correct if one is ever added.
#
# The eol=lf half is the part that does the work. text=auto alone
# normalises what is stored but checks out whatever the platform
# prefers, which leaves the working tree depending on each machine's
# core.autocrlf -- and a working tree that disagreed with the rest of
# the sources is what this is here to prevent. Addaptic.cpp arrived
# CRLF in the 2024 check-in, from the Windows era this repository
# still shows in its .gitignore, and sat that way unnoticed among
# twelve LF files until git diff --check started reporting every line
# of it as trailing whitespace.

* text=auto eol=lf
